<title>AUSTRIA: Brazil coffee co-op sees extra mild arabica demand.</title>
<headline>Brazil coffee co-op sees extra mild arabica demand.</headline>
<dateline>VIENNA 1997-06-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>A top Brazilian coffee body said on Tuesday it saw demand for 5-10 million extra bags of mild arabica over the next five to 10 years and forecast high quality coffee would continue to attract high prices.</p>
<p>&quot;We need at least 5-10 million bags more of high quality coffee in the next (five to 10) years,&quot; Joaquim Libanio Ferreira Leite, export director of Cooperativa Regional de Cafeicultores Em Guaxupe lta, told Reuters during a conference.</p>
<p>The association is Brazil's leading coffee growers' cooperative and the country's second biggest exporter.</p>
</text>
